          {
            title: 'Tri Palki',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tri Palki (Ð¢Ñ€Ð¸ Ð¿Ð°Ð»ÐºÐ¸, 'Three Sticks') is a Russian card game where players try to avoid busting past 31 points. Each player holds 4 cards and plays one card per turn, adding to a running total. If your card pushes the total over 31, you earn a 'palka' (stick). Three sticks and you're out.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Alexander Tvaladze describes a Russian version of the commerce game known as три палки (Three Sticks), a variant of the Schwimmen (31) family. The 31/commerce group is popular in Germany, Austria, and Russia; this Russian variant uses a 36-card pack and stick penalties for the lowest hand.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36 cards (6-A). Values: A=11, K=4, Q=3, J=2, 10=-10, 9=0, 6-8=Face value.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal 4 cards each.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
